<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Appomattox Court House</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1865</span> · Also known as Surrender at Appomattox · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-civil-war">American Civil War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Appomattox Court House, fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/virginia">Virginia</a> on 9 April 1865, was the last engagement of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/robert-e-lee">Robert E. Lee</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/army-of-northern-virginia">Army of Northern Virginia</a>. Cut off by Union forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulysses-s-grant">Ulysses S. Grant</a> after the fall of Richmond, Lee surrendered that day on generous terms. The surrender led to the collapse of the Confederacy within weeks.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-appomattox-court-house.jpg" alt="Battle of Appomattox Court House" width="320" height="195" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Thomas Nast · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:General_Robert_E._Lee_surrenders_at_Appomattox_Court_House_1865.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
